Add `Current state`, `implementation details`, `acceptance criteria` for `design/feature_descriptions/F_175_attach_files_to_card.md`.&#x20;
update the field `status` in the markdown feature description file to `ready for implementation`.

Read all referenced files before you begin except `agents` files. it is possible that the file is not yet written. &#x20;
Ask any question if something is ambiguous or not yet clear.
Be brief, but never compress away the subject, timing, or causal chain. Define ambiguous technical phrases. use $caveman skill.

Do not stage or commit changes. You have no need for get at this time.

design\CODEMAP.md:22:- Preload: [desktop/src/shell/preload.js](../desktop/src/shell/preload.js) — set in `webPreferences.preload` at [main.js:219](../desktop/main.js#L219). `sandbox: true`, `contextIsolation: true`, `nodeIntegration: false`.
design\CODEMAP.md:123:- Comments explain **why**, are sparse, often reference a feature id (`F-045`, `B_030`) tying code to `design/feature_descriptions/`.
design\architecture\architectural_decisions.md:29:| Card UI subscribes at field level. | A component subscribes only to the primitive or stable reference it renders, using granular `EventTarget` events and `useSyncExternalStore`. Do not clone or stringify a complete card to detect a field change. Group fields only in a deliberately small, stable projection when they are always rendered together. | A one-field change allocates and rerenders only what consumes that field, keeping memory use bounded and the UI responsive. |
design\architecture\architectural_decisions.md:30:| Cards are serialized only at persistence boundaries. | Mutate the owned `Card` through a focused operation, then serialize its current state when the persistence batch flushes. Editor changes update only the edited field. Activity linking updates only activity references. External file changes are parsed and applied deliberately without replacing dirty local state. | Persistence remains deterministic while concurrent saves and external updates cannot discard unrelated newer values. |
